  "title": "A removal orients the tree of cuts, and held cuts compose as iterated 2-sums",
  "subject": "How the knots a knot space keeps after one line is removed are organized along the tree of cuts of a space glued from several pieces",
  "conclusion": "Removing a line holds every cut pointing toward it and opens every cut pointing away; beyond a held cut nothing depends on the removal. The knots crossing only held cuts are exactly the iterated 2-sums, through held hubs, of knots crossing no cut, so new emergence lives only across opened cuts.",
